& [CurrentAuthorityAudit] distinguishes fact from formation
  + ParticipantAddress, AuthorityGrant, CommissionContract, WorkPacket, deterministic transcript admission, and EffectBroker role are implemented under the supervised mock-loop boundary
  + RuntimeGeneration and resident service sharing are implemented as immutable semantic execution substrate without sessions
  + TransportableSemanticState is signed formation with implementation authority limited to existing bounded fixtures and no general embodied cursor implementation
  + Metaattention learning, faculty runtime, narrative activation, and cooperative junction supply later semantic patterns but do not authorize CEA-001 runtime code
  + no current implementation defines EmbodiedAgentIdentity, environment identity, endpoint identity, embodiment session, or physical binding
  = must: reuse compatible SemanticId, ContentDigest, authority-containment, participant, and fault principles without claiming the present types already satisfy CEA-001

& [PassedBoundaryChecks] are material
  + Minecraft and NeoForge implementation types remain outside Cantor core
  + claim validation remains distinct from adapter admission, endpoint availability, physical binding, and effect authority
  + provider job identity remains disposable and subordinate to logical agent identity
  + shared immutable runtime state remains distinct from per-agent and per-session state
  + resume creates a predecessor-linked new session instead of reviving a terminal session identity
  + no I/O, clock, adapter, model, persistence, or effect is selected

& [BlockingIdentityStateCollision] violates data identity
  + EmbodiedAgentIdentity is declared stable while containing purpose_contract_digest, program_set_digest, authority_projection_digest, and lifecycle that may legitimately change
  + EnvironmentIdentity contains adapter_profile_digest and instance_descriptor_digest that may change across compatible upgrades or instance revisions
  + EmbodimentSessionIdentity contains lifecycle, so one session identity would resolve to incompatible content after every accepted transition
  + SemanticStateCursor and EpisodeCursor contain mutable disposition labels despite being described as immutable progress references
  + EmbodimentBindingClaim embeds complete current records rather than binding stable keys to exact record revisions
  + identity_collision faults cannot solve a model that creates collisions during normal lifecycle progression
  = conclusion: the source conflates natural identity keys, versioned definition records, and mutable lifecycle snapshots

& [RequiredCorrection] is structural rather than cosmetic
  + stable AgentKey, EnvironmentKey, EndpointKey, and SessionKey must contain only durable identity coordinates
  + AgentDefinitionRevision must carry purpose, program set, maximum authority, predecessor definition, and content digest
  + AgentRuntimeSnapshot must carry lifecycle, exact definition revision, semantic cursor, optional episode cursor, and active session reference
  + EnvironmentRevision and EndpointRevision must carry adapter, descriptor, policy, generation, kind, locator, and sharing details
  + SessionSnapshot must carry lifecycle, exact agent, environment, endpoint, definition and policy revisions, predecessor session, prior snapshot digest, and monotonic transition sequence
  + cursors must be immutable references; whether they are current, superseded, or invalid belongs in the containing snapshot or a separate status record
  + BindingClaim must reference stable keys plus exact revision and snapshot digests rather than nesting mutable identities
  + global uniqueness and exclusive endpoint ownership must remain later registry or adapter proofs rather than pure-form claims

& [RequirementImpact] is bounded
  + CEA1-001 through CEA1-014 remain the candidate obligation identities
  + CEA1-001, CEA1-002, CEA1-004, CEA1-006, and CEA1-009 require corrected record boundaries
  + all purpose, authority, claim-versus-proof, provider-neutral, fault, non-effect, and verification intentions remain valid
  + no new feature or effect is added by the correction

